(out/'review-explanation.md').write_text('''# Independent description review B\n\nRun: `physics-current3-blind-b-20261115-52b38f`  \nAgent task: `/root/physics_three_d_blind_b`\n\nThis is a first-pass review of the three fingerprint-bound current descriptions in the assigned order. The reviewer used the named round-b prompt, physics criteria, record schema, campaign, batch and bundle manifest, the shared pin-only seal, and the native book model/PDF/render manifest referenced by that bundle. No other reviewer output, previous description round, canonical diff, broad repository history, active source file or active QA file was read. The bound current V2 profile bodies were read as context and evaluated directly. Their historical review metadata and approval status were not treated as authority.\n\nAll three descriptions are kept. This is an independently reached candidate judgment, not a requested outcome. Each record provides a newly formulated bilingual chain that identifies the relevant physical understanding, an independently observable performance and a meaningfully changed transfer case. No replacement descriptions are present. The current profiles already articulate the respective understanding, performance and transfer requirements, so all three profile recommendations are `none`.\n\nFor significant figures, the central distinction is between displayed calculator digits and precision supported by data. Guard digits and justified final rounding form one coherent competence. A transfer from implicit written precision to explicit uncertainty stays within the description; deriving uncertainty propagation is not added.\n\nFor current, the cross-section, net transported charge and averaging interval give the formula its meaning. A changed case with return transport or a pause makes net accounting and interval choice visible. No instantaneous-current calculus is added.\n\nFor doping, the supplied simple bond model supports complementary donor and acceptor explanations. Charge balance joins mobile carriers with fixed ions; tracking a moved vacancy tests hole mobility without mistaking a hole for a proton. Neither band theory nor the p-n junction is added.\n\nThe actual PDF has five physical pages: physical pages 1 and 2 are the cover and navigation; physical pages 3, 4 and 5 are numbered learner pages 1, 2 and 3. All five rendered physical pages were actually viewed with the image tool. The three learner-page illustrations were seen: the significant-figure table and addition rounding example; the charge/current cross-section and 6 C/3 s example; and the n/p charge-carrier symbol diagram after ionisation. These are teaching supports and were not counted as learner demonstrations.\n\nThe PDF was rendered at 130 dpi with `pdftoppm`. The retained `book-physical-1.png` through `book-physical-5.png` are the exact page renderings passed to the image tool. No illustration was edited.\n\nThe supplied book is a three-goal review view. Raw applicability and the bare KC reference do not establish nationwide effective learner-facing projections or complete official source mappings. This review does not claim those external checks, human approval, learner acquisition, real experiments or release authority.\n\nValidation is limited to the supplied JSON Schema, exact assigned goal order, exact copied campaign/book/bundle/goal/page/current-text bindings, and immutable raw input hashes. Outputs are separate from active curriculum and QA files.\n''')
